  "articleBody": "So, you're dreaming of a beautiful new tile floor in your bathroom? Awesome! But before you pick out your favorite tiles, let's talk about what goes on underneath. Proper preparation of your bathroom subfloor is probably the most crucial step for a long-lasting, problem-free tile installation. You can't just slap tile down on any old surface! First, you need to make sure the subfloor is clean, level, and structurally sound enough to support the weight of the tile. Any significant dips, bumps, or weak spots will eventually telegraph through your new tile, leading to cracks or loose pieces. Next, confirm the structural adequacy of your subfloor and joists. Some older homes or certain types of subflooring might not be robust enough for heavy tile, especially natural stone, without additional reinforcement. Once that's all checked out, you'll establish your reference lines to ensure a straight and visually appealing layout. Only then can the mortar be spread and the tiles set with proper spacers. Rushing this prep stage is a recipe for disaster. If you're unsure about your subfloor's condition, or if you suspect any issues like deflection or damage, it's always best to consult with experienced professionals, like Abraham Becerra and his team at HH Remodeling LLC. They can properly assess your floor and get it perfectly ready for its new tile.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
